In Go 1.21, the loop variable `i` is a single variable that is reused on each iteration. Your goroutines capture `i` by reference, not by value. By the time the goroutines run, the loop has already finished, so `i` is `5`.

Fix it by passing the current loop value into the goroutine:

<solution language="go" verdict="fix">
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"sync"
)

func main() {
	var wg sync.WaitGroup
	for i := 0; i < 5; i++ {
		wg.Add(1)
		go func(j int) {
			defer wg.Done()
			fmt.Println(j)
		}(i)
	}
	wg.Wait()
}
</solution>

